      {
        "id": 202023,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-08-26T13:15:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I feel like there's a big thematic shift in tone between the two games. Spirit Island seems to cast certain nationalities as the enemy, while Sentinels bases being a good or bad guy solely on the individual and there's no thematic issues presented regards stuff like Legacy being proud of his national heritage.</p><p>And in Sentinels the Nexus is used as a source of power <em>by</em> humanity to protect humanity from Bad Things, while in Spirit Island it seems like you're mostly protecting the \"Nexus\" <em>from</em> humanity.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:30:39.387Z",
